      "body": "## Problem\n\nHiSparse prefill randomly crashes with `CUDA error: an illegal memory access` in `sparse_mla_attention.forward_mqa` → `_forward_mqa_kernel` on the staged prefill cache. `HiSparseRuntime.gather_prefill_cache` stages a request's KV into an exact-size buffer (often 1–3 blocks of 64 rows), and FlashInfer's trtllm-gen sparse MLA decode kernel reads ~170–250 rows from the start of its KV cache regardless of the cache's size or the top-k indices (flashinfer-ai/flashinfer#6484). It faults whenever the caching allocator puts the staged buffer near an unmapped page. Surfaced in #61487 (HiSparse + DBO); DBO makes it more frequent but it is not DBO-specific.\n\n## Fix\n\nAllocate at least 256 rows behind the staged buffer and return the exact-size view, so all downstream shapes are unchanged. Cost: ≤168 KB of transient allocation per staged layer.\n\n## Test plan\n\nHardware: 4x B200 pod (pirate2 dell-b200-01), flashinfer 0.7.0.post1, torch 2.13.0+cu130, CUDA 13.0. vLLM `2f18d13cf` (main at the time the env was built) with and without this PR's diff.\n\nRepro (DP2 + EP + DBO, eager, GLM-5.3 NVFP4 with dummy weights, 8 layers; `crash.sh` starts the server below and sends 3 rounds of 128 concurrent 30-word completions with `max_tokens=128`):\n\n```bash\nvllm serve RedHatAI/GLM-5.3-NVFP4 --load-format dummy --hf-overrides '{\"num_hidden_layers\": 8}' \\\n  -tp 1 -dp 2 --enable-expert-parallel --enable-dbo --all2all-backend deepep_low_latency \\\n  --kv-cache-dtype fp8 --block-size 64 --max-model-len 8192 \\\n  --attention-config '{\"hisparse_config\":{}}' \\\n  --kv-transfer-config '{\"kv_connector\":\"HiSparseConnector\",\"kv_role\":\"kv_both\",\"kv_connector_extra_config\":{\"host_pool_gib\":24}}' \\\n  --dbo-decode-token-threshold 2 --dbo-prefill-token-threshold 512 --compilation-config '{\"cudagraph_mode\":\"NONE\"}'\n# env: VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER=1\n```\n\n| Revision | Servers | Load rounds (128 req each) | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| main | 2 | 1st server: round 1; 2nd server (`CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1`): round 2 | illegal memory access, engine dead. With launch blocking the trace points at `sparse_mla_attention.py:858` (`_forward_mqa_kernel` on the `stage_prefill_rows` cache) → `trtllm_batch_decode_with_kv_cache_mla` |\n| main + this PR | 3 | 3 × 3 | 1152/1152 requests 200, no errors |\n\nUnit tests (B200):\n\n```bash\npytest tests/v1/attention/test_sparse_mla_backends.py -k \"hisparse or HiSparse or staging\"   # 40 passed\npytest tests/v1/kv_connector/unit/test_hisparse_connector.py                              # 15 passed\n```\n\nThe new `test_hisparse_staged_prefill_cache_backs_min_attention_rows` fails without the fix and passes with it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
